# Who must review a change. GitHub asks the owner of the last pattern that matches a file; "Require review from Code
# Owners" in the rules for main makes that review required. GOVERNANCE.md says who the people are. An owner is a user or
# a team: @Genterai, the organization the first-party readers name as theirs, cannot be asked for a review, so the owner
# stands for it. A line for a file that is not in the tree yet holds from the pull request that adds it.

# What decides what is read, marked and sent, and what Genter Cloud imports from npm at an exact version
/src/memory.js                  @dangenter
/src/readers.js                 @dangenter
/src/net.js                     @dangenter
/src/lexical.js                 @dangenter
/src/local.js                   @dangenter
/src/http.js                    @dangenter
/readers/reader.schema.json     @dangenter

# First-party readers and rules. A reader a person adds may bring a line of its own here, in the pull request that adds
# it, naming the owner its reader.json names (test/community.test.js checks: [owner-review]); from then on its owner
# reviews it. With no line, the maintainers review it: a reader needs no line, and no brief.
/readers/adr/                   @dangenter
/readers/banners/               @dangenter
/readers/changelog/             @dangenter
/readers/decisions/             @dangenter
/readers/obsidian/              @dangenter
/readers/rfc/                   @dangenter
/rules/en.json                  @dangenter
/rules/ru.json                  @dangenter

# What clients and people run: how they start Genter, where it is listed, and what a release ships (the image the
# release job publishes is built from the Dockerfile)
/Dockerfile                     @dangenter
/docker-compose.yml             @dangenter
/server.json                    @dangenter
/manifest.json                  @dangenter
/glama.json                     @dangenter
/.claude-plugin/                @dangenter
/plugins/                       @dangenter
/skills/                        @dangenter

# What the project promises and who decides
/STEWARDSHIP.md                 @dangenter
/TRADEMARKS.md                  @dangenter
/GOVERNANCE.md                  @dangenter
/ip-boundary.md                 @dangenter
/SECURITY.md                    @dangenter
/LICENSE                        @dangenter
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @dangenter

# What runs in CI and on release: a pull request can change its own checks, so the owner reads those changes
/.github/                       @dangenter
